{"kind":"assert","text":"CJ-2 pagination, answer to 331ceaf1. Use one rule, not two: `next` always names the last examined Directory index lane, whether or not that lane listed an issue. It is a scan position, and `--after` already accepts it. A page with no issues then continues like any other page, and a page that ends on a non-issue lane does not rescan it. Keep incomplete/1 when the bound stops the scan. Keep a refused first lane retriable with no cursor. Change the design note's sentence \"next names the last listed issue\" to this rule in the CJ-2 head, and add a test for a full page of 100 lanes with no issue rows, and for a resume from its cursor.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}